      "writtenOn": "2019-05-02T17:36:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "fwiw, i don\u0027t see how hmac_drbg_generate_p256 can wind up doing non-word writes. It explicitly writes to the word members of p256_int. Is it due to the __packed attribute and a compiler that assumes worst case w/o analysis?\n\nThat packed attribute is ill-advised on that struct in general, I/O marshaling needs to be explicit imo. Why are we confident that cp8w won\u0027t feel like using the same byte copy at some point?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 817,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 817,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "56e7fd1b09f71ece1dd6ce39e7da5b6230b11bd1",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
