      "writtenOn": "2019-05-02T23:45:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes I believe that is correct; compiler assumes that the k_out parameter may not be aligned and uses strb to write (see disassembly of p256_add_d() in the doc as an example)\n\nThat said, it seems that in practise, hmac_drbg_generate_p256() didn\u0027t suffer from this problem, but the previous (RFC6979) implementation did.",
      "parentUuid": "90c044f5_cef5653f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 817,
        "startChar": 2,
